Error [jet.PointerAcrossCBoundary]: Type `*Int` cannot cross the C boundary here.
  --> tests/ui/cffi_e3202_ptr_boundary.jet:3:25
    |
  3 |     return_ptr: fn() -> *Int = "DemoReturnPtr"
    |                         ^^^^
 Why: C FFI allows by-value scalars and `String` in ordinary code; pointers and other gated types need `use core.mem` and an `#Unsafe { … }` region.
 Fix: Move the call inside `#Unsafe`, or change the type to a C-safe value type.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3202
